# Tailwind CSS Usage Rules for Next.js + Modus

## 🎯 Overview

This document outlines the proper usage of Tailwind CSS in Next.js applications with Modus Design System. The goal is to minimize custom CSS and use inline Tailwind classes with Modus colors for better maintainability and consistency.

## 🎨 Core Principles

### ✅ ALWAYS Use Inline Tailwind Classes

**Preferred Approach:**

```tsx
<div
  className="flex items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg border"
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)",
    borderColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)",
    color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)",
  }}
>
  Content
</div>
```

**Avoid Custom CSS Classes:**

```tsx
// ❌ Don't do this
<div className="custom-card">Content</div>
```

```css
/* ❌ Don't create custom CSS classes */
.custom-card {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 1rem;
  border-radius: 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--modus-wc-color-base-200);
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-page);
}
```

## 🎨 Modus Color Integration

### ✅ ONLY Use Modus CSS Variables for Colors

**Approved Modus Colors (9 total):**

```css
/* Base Colors (5 total) */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)     /* Background: #fff (light) / #000 (dark) */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-100)      /* Light gray: #f1f1f6 (light) / #252a2e (dark) */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)      /* Medium gray: #cbcdd6 (light) / #464b52 (dark) */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-300)      /* Dark gray: #b7b9c3 (light) / #353a40 (dark) */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)  /* Text: #171c1e (light) / #cbcdd6 (dark) */

/* Semantic Colors (4 total - same in both themes) */
var(--modus-wc-color-info)          /* Blue: #0063a3 */
var(--modus-wc-color-success)       /* Green: #1e8a44 */
var(--modus-wc-color-error)         /* Red: #da212c */
var(--modus-wc-color-warning)       /* Orange: #fbad26 */
```

### ✅ Correct Color Usage Pattern

```tsx
// ✅ Correct - Using Modus CSS variables with Tailwind classes
<div
  className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 rounded-lg border"
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)",
    borderColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)",
    color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)",
  }}
>
  <h2 style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)" }}>Title</h2>
  <p style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)", opacity: 0.8 }}>
    Description
  </p>
</div>
```

### ❌ NEVER Use These Color Approaches

```tsx
// ❌ Wrong - Hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-white text-black border-gray-300">
  Content
</div>

// ❌ Wrong - Tailwind color classes
<div className="bg-gray-100 text-gray-900 border-gray-200">
  Content
</div>

// ❌ Wrong - Custom CSS variables
<div style={{ backgroundColor: "var(--my-custom-color)" }}>
  Content
</div>
```

